cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite as below."
title: "AgroSense: Satellite-Based Crop Stress Classification and Smart Farming Decision Support for Pakistan Smallholder Agriculture"
authors:
  - family-names: Shahmeer
    given-names: Ali
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-19"
url: "https://github.com/ALI-SHAHMEER/agrosense-pakistan-crop-stress"
abstract: >
  AgroSense is a crop stress classification system that uses Sentinel-2
  satellite imagery collected via the Google Earth Engine API to classify
  Pakistani agricultural fields into spectrally derived crop-condition proxy
  classes (Healthy, Stressed, Diseased). This repository contains 1,786 real
  Sentinel-2 observations from 116 field sites across all four provinces of
  Pakistan over ten growing seasons (2015-2024). Labels are derived from a
  vegetation health composite and have not been independently validated against
  field diagnoses. The best model (SVM RBF) achieves 98.34% test accuracy
  under field-grouped evaluation (GroupShuffleSplit on location_id).
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - precision agriculture
  - crop stress
  - Sentinel-2
  - machine learning
  - Pakistan
  - Google Earth Engine
license: MIT
